package app.pantrypal

/** Fifty distinct slow-cooker dishes with measured ingredients and step-by-step methods.
 * Recipes are practical adaptations; publisher links are supplied where a matching reference recipe exists.
 */
internal object SlowCookerRecipes {
 private data class E(val title:String,val ingredients:String,val steps:String,val source:String,val cook:String="6–8 hours on LOW",val prep:String="15 minutes")
 private val e = listOf(
E("Slow-cooker beef stew","700g braising beef; 2 onions (about 200g); 3 carrots (about 300g); 500g potatoes; 500ml beef stock; 2 tbsp tomato purée; 1 tsp dried thyme; 2 tbsp plain flour","1. Cut beef into 3cm chunks and toss with flour and black pepper. Chop onion, slice carrots and celery, and cube potatoes.\n2. Brown beef in batches in 1 tbsp oil if time allows; transfer to the slow cooker. Soften onion in the same pan for 3–4 minutes.\n3. Add carrots, celery, potatoes, tomato purée, thyme and hot stock. Stir, cover and cook on LOW for 8–10 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until beef is fork-tender.\n4. Taste and season. If gravy is thin, stir in 1 tbsp cornflour mixed with 1 tbsp cold water and cook on HIGH for 15–20 minutes.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-beef-stew","7–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker sausage casserole","8 pork sausages (about 600g); 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 1 celery stick; 400g chopped tomatoes; 400g drained cannellini beans; 250ml stock; 2 tsp mixed dried herbs","1. Slice onion, cut carrots into thick pieces and slice celery.\n2. Brown sausages in a frying pan for 5–8 minutes, turning, then transfer to the slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, carrots, celery, tomatoes, drained beans, stock and herbs. Stir gently.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 6–8 hours or HIGH for 3–4 hours, until vegetables are tender and sausages are cooked through. Check seasoning.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-sausage-casserole","6–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker chilli con carne","500g beef mince; 1 onion (150g); 1 pepper (150g); 2 garlic cloves; 400g chopped tomatoes; 400g drained kidney beans; 150ml beef stock; 2 tsp chilli powder; 2 tsp ground cumin","1. Finely chop onion, pepper and garlic.\n2. Brown mince in a hot frying pan, breaking it into small pieces; transfer to the slow cooker.\n3. Soften onion and pepper in the pan for 4–5 minutes. Add garlic, cumin and chilli powder; cook for 30 seconds.\n4. Add tomatoes, drained kidney beans, stock and tomato purée. Stir well, cover and cook on LOW for 6–8 hours or HIGH for 3–4 hours.\n5. If too thick, add a splash of hot water; if too thin, cook uncovered on HIGH for 15–20 minutes. Season and serve with rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-chilli-con-carne","6–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker chicken casserole","8 chicken thighs (about 1kg); 1 onion (150g); 3 carrots (300g); 2 celery sticks; 500ml chicken stock; 1 tsp dried thyme; 1 bay leaf; 150g peas","1. Slice onion, cut carrots into chunky slices and slice celery.\n2. Put vegetables in the slow cooker and arrange chicken thighs on top. Add hot stock, thyme and bay leaf.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 2½–3½ hours, until the thickest part of each thigh reaches 75°C.\n4. Stir in peas for the final 20–30 minutes. Remove bay leaf, season and serve. Thicken sauce with 1 tbsp cornflour mixed with cold water if desired.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-chicken-casserole","6–7 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker beef stew with dumplings","600g stewing beef; 1 onion (150g); 3 carrots (300g); 2 potatoes (about 300g); 500ml beef stock; 2 tbsp tomato purée; 150g self-raising flour; 75g suet; 6–8 tbsp cold water for dumplings","1. Toss beef with flour and black pepper. Cut potatoes and carrots into chunks and chop onion.\n2. Brown beef in batches if possible. Transfer to the slow cooker with vegetables, tomato purée, thyme and hot stock.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until beef is tender.\n4. Mix self-raising flour and suet with a pinch of salt and 6 tbsp cold water, adding a little more only if needed, to make a soft dough. Shape into 8 dumplings.\n5. Place dumplings on top, replace the lid and cook on HIGH for 45–60 minutes without lifting the lid, until risen and cooked through. Check seasoning.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-beef-stew-with-dumplings","7–8 hours on LOW","25 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker pulled pork","1–1.2kg pork shoulder; 1 onion (150g); 150ml apple juice; 3 tbsp barbecue sauce; 1 tbsp cider vinegar; 1 tsp smoked paprika","1. Slice onion and place in the slow cooker. Pat pork dry and sit it on top, fat-side up.\n2. Mix apple juice, barbecue sauce, cider vinegar and smoked paprika; pour around the pork.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 8–10 hours or HIGH for 5–6 hours, until pork shreds easily with two forks.\n4. Transfer pork to a dish, remove large pieces of fat and shred. Skim excess fat from the cooking liquid, then mix enough sauce through the meat to coat.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-pulled-pork","8–10 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker beef bourguignon","700g stewing beef; 100g bacon lardons; 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 200g mushrooms; 250ml red wine; 250ml beef stock; 1 tsp dried thyme","1. Cut beef into 3cm chunks; slice onion and carrots and halve mushrooms.\n2. Brown bacon in a frying pan, then brown beef in batches. Transfer to the slow cooker.\n3. Soften onion and carrots in the pan for 4 minutes. Add wine and simmer for 2 minutes, scraping up browned bits. Tip into cooker with stock, mushrooms and thyme.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until beef is tender. Thicken sauce if needed and season to taste.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-beef-bourguignon","7–8 hours on LOW","25 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker beef brisket","1kg beef brisket; 2 onions (300g); 3 carrots (300g); 400ml beef stock; 1 tbsp Worcestershire sauce; 2 tbsp tomato purée; 1 tsp dried thyme","1. Slice onions and cut carrots into thick chunks. Arrange in the bottom of the slow cooker.\n2. Season brisket with black pepper. Mix stock, Worcestershire sauce, tomato purée and thyme; pour around the meat.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 8–9 hours or HIGH for 5–6 hours, until fork-tender.\n4. Rest for 10–15 minutes, then slice across the grain. Skim fat from juices and spoon over the meat.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-brisket-with-golden-ale-gravy-horseradish-mash","8–9 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker beef tacos","800g beef chuck; 1 onion (150g); 2 garlic cloves; 200ml beef stock; 2 tbsp tomato purée; 2 tsp smoked paprika; 2 tsp ground cumin; 8 small tortillas","1. Slice onion and finely chop garlic. Mix stock, tomato purée, paprika and cumin.\n2. Cut beef into large chunks and place over onion in the slow cooker. Pour over spice mixture.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 8–9 hours or HIGH for 5–6 hours, until beef shreds easily.\n4. Shred beef into the juices. If watery, cook uncovered on HIGH for 15–20 minutes. Serve in warmed tortillas with toppings.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-beef-tacos","8 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker beef curry","700g stewing beef; 1 onion (150g); 3 tbsp mild curry paste; 400g chopped tomatoes; 200ml beef stock; 2 carrots (200g); 2 garlic cloves","1. Cut beef into 3cm chunks and slice onion. Finely chop garlic.\n2. Brown beef in batches if possible; transfer to slow cooker.\n3. Stir curry paste with garlic, tomatoes and stock, then pour over beef. Add onion and sliced carrots.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until beef is tender. Reduce sauce uncovered on HIGH if needed; season and serve with rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","7–8 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker beef stroganoff","600g beef strips; 1 onion (150g); 250g mushrooms; 250ml beef stock; 1 tbsp Dijon mustard; 1 tsp paprika; 150g soured cream","1. Slice onion and mushrooms. Cut beef into strips if needed.\n2. Brown beef quickly in batches; transfer to slow cooker with onion and mushrooms.\n3. Stir stock, mustard and paprika together and pour over. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 2½–3½ hours, until tender.\n4. If needed, stir in 1 tbsp cornflour mixed with cold water and cook on HIGH for 10–15 minutes. Turn off heat and stir in soured cream; do not boil after adding it.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","6–8 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow-cooker beef goulash","700g stewing beef; 1 onion (150g); 2 peppers (300g); 2 garlic cloves; 400g chopped tomatoes; 250ml beef stock; 2 tbsp sweet paprika","1. Cut beef into 3cm chunks, slice onion and peppers, and finely chop garlic.\n2. Brown beef in batches if possible and place in the slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, peppers, garlic, tomatoes, stock and sweet paprika. Stir to combine.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until beef is tender. Taste before adding salt, as stock may be salty.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","7–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker butter chicken","700g chicken thighs; 1 onion (150g); 2 garlic cloves; 3 tbsp mild curry paste; 400g chopped tomatoes; 100ml chicken stock; 100ml double cream; 25g butter","1. Cut chicken into large bite-sized pieces and slice onion. Crush garlic.\n2. Put chicken, onion, garlic, curry paste, tomatoes and stock in the slow cooker; stir to coat.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C in the thickest pieces.\n4. Stir in butter and cream for the final 20–30 minutes. Taste and season; serve with rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker chicken korma","700g chicken thighs; 1 onion (150g); 3 tbsp korma paste; 200ml chicken stock; 200ml coconut milk; 2 tbsp ground almonds; 2 tbsp chopped fresh coriander","1. Cut chicken into large bite-sized pieces and slice onion.\n2. Add chicken, onion, korma paste and stock to the slow cooker. Stir to coat.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C.\n4. Stir in coconut milk and ground almonds for the final 30 minutes. Add coriander, taste and season; serve with rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker chicken tikka masala","700g chicken thighs; 1 onion (150g); 3 tbsp tikka paste; 400g chopped tomatoes; 100ml chicken stock; 100ml double cream; 2 tbsp chopped fresh coriander","1. Cut chicken into large bite-sized pieces and slice onion.\n2. Put chicken, onion, tikka paste, tomatoes and stock in the slow cooker and stir.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C.\n4. Stir in cream for the final 20 minutes. Taste, season and scatter with coriander.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker lamb curry","700g diced lamb; 1 onion (150g); 3 tbsp curry paste; 400g chopped tomatoes; 200ml lamb stock; 3 garlic cloves; 1 tbsp grated ginger","1. Cut lamb into 3cm chunks. Chop onion, finely chop garlic and grate ginger.\n2. Brown lamb in batches if possible; transfer to slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, garlic, ginger, curry paste, tomatoes and stock. Stir well.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until lamb is tender. Taste and season; serve with rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-lamb","7–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker lamb tagine","700g diced lamb; 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 100g dried apricots; 400g chopped tomatoes; 250ml lamb stock; 2 tsp ground cumin; 2 tsp ground coriander; 1 tsp ground cinnamon","1. Cut lamb into 3cm chunks, slice onion and carrots, and halve larger apricots.\n2. Brown lamb in batches if possible, then transfer to the slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, carrots, apricots, tomatoes, stock, cumin, coriander and cinnamon. Stir.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until lamb is tender. Reduce sauce uncovered on HIGH if needed; serve with couscous.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-lamb","7–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker lamb shoulder","1–1.3kg lamb shoulder; 4 garlic cloves; 2 onions (300g); 2 rosemary sprigs; 200ml lamb stock; 1 tsp ground black pepper","1. Slice onions and place in slow cooker with rosemary. Make small cuts in lamb and tuck in slivers of garlic.\n2. Sit lamb on onions, add stock and black pepper, then cover.\n3. Cook on LOW for 8–9 hours or HIGH for 5–6 hours, until very tender and pulling away from the bone.\n4. Rest for 15 minutes before carving or pulling apart. Skim excess fat from juices.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-lamb-shoulder","8–9 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow-cooker lamb shanks","4 lamb shanks (about 1.2kg); 2 carrots (200g); 1 onion (150g); 3 garlic cloves; 400g chopped tomatoes; 400ml lamb stock; 2 tbsp tomato purée; 2 rosemary sprigs","1. Slice onion, cut carrots into chunks and finely chop garlic.\n2. Brown shanks in a hot frying pan, turning to colour all sides, then place in the slow cooker.\n3. Add carrots, onion, garlic, tomatoes, stock, tomato purée and rosemary.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 8–9 hours or HIGH for 5–6 hours, until meat is very tender. Skim fat and season the sauce.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-lamb","8–9 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker Moroccan lamb stew","650g diced lamb; 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 400g drained chickpeas; 400g chopped tomatoes; 300ml lamb stock; 2 tsp ground cumin; 1 tsp paprika; 1 tsp ground cinnamon","1. Cut lamb into 3cm chunks, slice onion and carrots, and drain and rinse chickpeas.\n2. Brown lamb in batches if possible. Transfer to slow cooker with vegetables and chickpeas.\n3. Add tomatoes, stock, cumin, paprika and cinnamon; stir.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until lamb and carrots are tender. Season and serve with couscous.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-lamb","7–8 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker pork casserole","700g diced pork; 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 1 apple (150g); 300ml chicken stock; 1 tbsp wholegrain mustard; 1 tsp dried thyme","1. Cut pork into 3cm chunks. Slice onion, cut carrots into chunks and core and chop apple.\n2. Brown pork in batches if possible, then transfer to the slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, carrots, apple, stock, mustard and thyme. Stir.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until pork is tender and thoroughly cooked. Season and serve with mash.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-pork-casserole","7–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker gammon in cola","1–1.2kg gammon joint; 1 litre cola (or enough to mostly cover); 1 onion (150g); 2 bay leaves; 1 tsp peppercorns; 1 tbsp mustard (optional)","1. Put sliced onion and bay leaves in the slow cooker. Add gammon and peppercorns, then pour in cola to roughly halfway to two-thirds up the joint; do not overfill.\n2. Cover and cook on LOW for 6–8 hours, following pack and appliance guidance, until the centre reaches at least 70°C for 2 minutes or the pack's higher specified temperature.\n3. Lift out carefully and rest for 10 minutes. Remove rind if glazing, brush with mustard if using, and grill briefly until golden, watching closely. Slice to serve.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-gammon","6–8 hours on LOW","10 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker gammon","1–1.2kg gammon joint; 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 2 bay leaves; 1 tsp peppercorns; 750ml water or stock (add more to reach halfway up joint)","1. Put sliced onion, carrots, bay leaves and peppercorns in the slow cooker. Add gammon and pour in water or stock to reach about halfway up the joint.\n2. Cover and cook on LOW for 6–8 hours, following pack and appliance guidance, until the centre reaches at least 70°C for 2 minutes or the pack's higher specified temperature.\n3. Rest for 10 minutes before slicing. Skim excess fat from cooking liquid.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","6–8 hours on LOW","10 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker Spanish chicken","8 chicken thighs (about 1kg); 150g chorizo; 1 onion (150g); 2 peppers (300g); 400g chopped tomatoes; 75g pitted olives; 150ml chicken stock; 1 tsp smoked paprika","1. Slice onion and peppers. Cut chorizo into thick slices.\n2. Fry chorizo for 3–4 minutes to release its oil. Transfer chorizo and oil to the slow cooker.\n3. Add chicken, onion, peppers, tomatoes, olives, stock and paprika. Stir around the chicken.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 2½–3½ hours, until chicken reaches 75°C. Season carefully because chorizo and stock are salty.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-spanish-chicken","6–7 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow-cooker roast chicken","1 whole chicken (1.3–1.6kg, sized to fit); 1 onion (150g); 1 lemon; 4 garlic cloves; 4 thyme sprigs; 1 tsp ground black pepper","1. Check that the chicken fits with the lid fully closed and follow your slow cooker's instructions for whole poultry; do not use a bird too large for the pot.\n2. Slice onion thickly and place in the base. Pat chicken dry, season with pepper, and put lemon, garlic and thyme inside the cavity. Sit chicken breast-side up on onion.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for the appliance-recommended time (often around 5–6 hours for a 1.3–1.6kg bird). Check with a thermometer that the thickest breast and inner thigh reach 75°C.\n4. For crisp skin, transfer to a roasting tray and grill briefly until golden. Rest for 10–15 minutes before carving. Do not serve unless safely cooked.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-roast-chicken","Check appliance guidance","10 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker coq au vin","8 chicken thighs (about 1kg); 150g bacon lardons; 1 onion (150g); 200g mushrooms; 2 carrots (200g); 250ml red wine; 250ml chicken stock; 1 tsp dried thyme","1. Slice onion and carrots and halve mushrooms.\n2. Brown bacon in a frying pan; remove. Brown chicken thighs, then transfer both to the slow cooker.\n3. Soften onion and carrots in the pan. Add wine and simmer for 2 minutes, then pour into cooker with stock, mushrooms and thyme.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 3–4 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C and is tender. Thicken sauce if needed and season.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-coq-au-vin","6–7 hours on LOW","25 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker chicken chasseur","8 chicken thighs (about 1kg); 1 onion (150g); 200g mushrooms; 400g chopped tomatoes; 250ml chicken stock; 2 garlic cloves; 1 tsp dried thyme","1. Slice onion and mushrooms and finely chop garlic.\n2. If desired, brown chicken thighs in a hot pan, then transfer to slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, mushrooms, tomatoes, stock, garlic and thyme. Stir around chicken.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 3–3½ hours, until chicken reaches 75°C. Thicken sauce if needed and season.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","6–7 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker honey mustard chicken","8 chicken thighs (about 1kg); 3 tbsp honey; 2 tbsp wholegrain mustard; 150ml chicken stock; 2 garlic cloves; 1 onion (150g)","1. Slice onion and finely chop garlic. Arrange onion in the slow cooker and place chicken on top.\n2. Whisk honey, mustard, stock and garlic together; pour over chicken.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C.\n4. If sauce is thin, cook uncovered on HIGH for 10–15 minutes or stir in 1 tsp cornflour mixed with cold water. Taste and season.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker pulled chicken","800g chicken thighs; 1 onion (150g); 150ml barbecue sauce; 100ml chicken stock; 1 tsp smoked paprika; 1 tbsp cider vinegar","1. Slice onion and place in the slow cooker. Add chicken thighs.\n2. Mix barbecue sauce, stock, paprika and cider vinegar; pour over chicken.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C and pulls apart easily.\n4. Shred chicken with two forks and return to sauce. If sauce is thin, cook uncovered on HIGH for 10–15 minutes. Serve in rolls, wraps or with rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW"),
E("White chicken chilli","700g chicken thighs; 1 onion (150g); 2 garlic cloves; 2 x 400g tins cannellini beans, drained; 500ml chicken stock; 2 tsp ground cumin; 150g cream cheese","1. Chop onion and garlic. Drain and rinse cannellini beans.\n2. Add chicken, onion, garlic, beans, stock and cumin to the slow cooker. Stir gently.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C.\n4. Remove chicken and shred with two forks; return to pot. Stir in cream cheese until melted. Add a splash of hot water if too thick; season and serve.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/white-chicken-chilli","5–6 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker chicken soup","500g chicken thighs; 3 carrots (300g); 2 celery sticks; 1 onion (150g); 1.2 litres chicken stock; 1 bay leaf; 100g small pasta (optional)","1. Chop onion, carrots and celery. Put vegetables in the slow cooker with chicken, stock and bay leaf.\n2. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 3–4 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C and vegetables are tender.\n3. Lift out chicken, remove bones if present and shred meat. Return to soup and remove bay leaf.\n4. If using pasta, add it for the packet's cooking time, usually the final 15–25 minutes on HIGH. Add boiling water if needed and season.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","6–7 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker bolognese","500g beef mince; 1 onion (150g); 1 carrot (100g); 1 celery stick; 2 garlic cloves; 500g passata; 2 tbsp tomato purée; 2 tsp dried oregano","1. Finely chop onion, carrot, celery and garlic.\n2. Brown mince in batches, breaking it up well. Transfer to the slow cooker.\n3. Soften onion, carrot and celery in the pan for 4–5 minutes. Add garlic for 30 seconds, then stir in passata, tomato purée and oregano.\n4. Pour sauce over mince and stir thoroughly. Cover and cook on LOW for 6–8 hours or HIGH for 3–4 hours. If watery, cook uncovered on HIGH for 15–20 minutes. Season and serve with pasta.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-spaghetti-bolognese","6–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Campfire stew","400g smoked sausages; 150g bacon; 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 400g baked beans; 400g chopped tomatoes; 250ml stock; 1 tsp smoked paprika","1. Slice sausages, chop bacon and onion, and cut carrots into chunks.\n2. Brown bacon and sausages in a frying pan if possible. Transfer to slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, carrots, baked beans, tomatoes, stock and paprika. Stir well.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 3 hours, until carrots are tender and sausages cooked through. Season carefully because smoked meat and beans can be salty.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/campfire-stew","6–7 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker turkey curry","700g turkey thigh, diced; 1 onion (150g); 3 tbsp curry paste; 400g chopped tomatoes; 200ml coconut milk; 100ml stock; 1 green pepper (150g)","1. Cut turkey into even 3cm chunks and slice onion and pepper.\n2. Brown turkey in batches if possible and transfer to slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, pepper, curry paste, tomatoes and stock. Stir to coat.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until turkey reaches 75°C. Stir in coconut milk for the final 20–30 minutes. Season and serve with rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW"),
E("Slow cooker beef and ale pie filling","700g stewing beef; 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 300ml brown ale; 200ml beef stock; 2 tbsp tomato purée; 1 tsp dried thyme; 1 sheet ready-rolled puff pastry (about 320g)","1. Cut beef into 3cm chunks and toss with flour and black pepper. Slice onion and carrots.\n2. Brown beef in batches, then transfer to slow cooker with onion and carrots.\n3. Add ale, stock, tomato purée and thyme. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until beef is tender. If sauce is thin, cook uncovered on HIGH for 15–20 minutes.\n4. Cool filling until no longer steaming. Spoon into pie dish, cover with pastry and seal edges. Cut a steam hole and bake according to pastry packet until golden and piping hot.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","7–8 hours on LOW","25 minutes"),
E("Vegetable stew with cheddar dumplings","1 leek (150g); 3 carrots (300g); 3 potatoes (450g); 1 courgette (200g); 150g peas; 600ml vegetable stock; 1 tbsp Dijon mustard; 150g self-raising flour; 75g grated cheddar; 6–8 tbsp cold water","1. Wash and slice leek; cut carrots, potatoes and courgette into similar-sized chunks.\n2. Put vegetables (except peas), stock and mustard into slow cooker. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until nearly tender.\n3. Mix flour and cheddar with a pinch of salt and 6 tbsp cold water, adding only enough extra water to make a soft dough. Shape into 8 dumplings.\n4. Stir in peas and place dumplings on top. Cover and cook on HIGH for 45–60 minutes without lifting lid, until dumplings are cooked through. Thicken stew if needed.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/spring-veg-stew-cheddar-dumplings","5–6 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker vegetable lasagne","1 aubergine (300g); 1 courgette (200g); 1 pepper (150g); 500g passata; 2 tsp dried oregano; 6–8 lasagne sheets (about 150g); 250g ricotta; 150g grated mozzarella","1. Dice aubergine, courgette and pepper. Mix with passata, oregano and 100ml water; season.\n2. Spread a thin layer of sauce in a greased slow-cooker pot. Add lasagne sheets, sauce and small dollops of ricotta in layers, finishing with sauce and mozzarella. Keep pasta covered by sauce.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 3–4 hours, checking from 3 hours until pasta is tender and the centre is piping hot. Avoid lifting the lid repeatedly.\n4. Switch off and stand for 15 minutes before slicing. This is softer than oven-baked lasagne.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","3–4 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Spiced root and lentil casserole","200g red lentils; 2 carrots (200g); 1 parsnip (150g); 1 onion (150g); 400g chopped tomatoes; 750ml vegetable stock; 2 tsp ground cumin; 1 tsp paprika","1. Rinse lentils. Dice onion, carrots and parsnip into small, even pieces.\n2. Add lentils, vegetables, tomatoes, stock, cumin and paprika to the slow cooker and stir.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 3–4 hours, until lentils and vegetables are soft. Add hot water if too thick.\n4. Taste, season with salt and pepper, and add a squeeze of lemon if available.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-sunday-lunch","5–6 hours on LOW"),
E("Pasta e fagioli","1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 2 celery sticks; 2 garlic cloves; 400g chopped tomatoes; 750ml vegetable stock; 400g drained cannellini beans; 150g small pasta; 1 tsp dried oregano","1. Finely chop onion, carrots, celery and garlic. Drain and rinse beans.\n2. Add vegetables, garlic, tomatoes, stock and oregano to slow cooker. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until vegetables are tender.\n3. Stir in beans and pasta for the pasta packet's cooking time, usually 15–25 minutes on HIGH. Add boiling water if needed; pasta absorbs liquid quickly.\n4. Check pasta is tender, season and serve promptly.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/pasta-e-fagioli","5–6 hours on LOW","15 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker lentil soup","250g red lentils; 2 carrots (200g); 1 onion (150g); 2 garlic cloves; 400g chopped tomatoes; 1 litre vegetable stock; 1 tsp ground cumin","1. Rinse lentils in a sieve. Finely chop onion, carrots and garlic.\n2. Put lentils, vegetables, tomatoes, stock and cumin into slow cooker and stir.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 3–4 hours, until lentils are completely soft. Add boiling water if too thick.\n4. Blend smooth or leave chunky. Taste and season with salt, pepper and lemon juice if desired.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","6–7 hours on LOW","10 minutes"),
E("Three-bean slow cooker chilli","1 onion (150g); 1 pepper (150g); 2 garlic cloves; 400g kidney beans, drained; 400g black beans, drained; 400g cannellini beans, drained; 400g chopped tomatoes; 2 tbsp tomato purée; 2 tsp chilli powder; 250ml vegetable stock","1. Finely chop onion, pepper and garlic. Drain and rinse all beans thoroughly.\n2. Add vegetables, beans, tomatoes, tomato purée, chilli powder and stock to slow cooker. Stir.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until vegetables are tender and sauce thickens.\n4. Mash a few beans against the pot to thicken if needed. Taste, season and serve with rice or tortilla chips.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW","15 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker mushroom stroganoff","600g mushrooms; 1 onion (150g); 2 garlic cloves; 250ml vegetable stock; 1 tbsp Dijon mustard; 1 tsp paprika; 150g crème fraîche","1. Slice mushrooms and onion; finely chop garlic.\n2. Put mushrooms, onion, garlic, stock, mustard and paprika in slow cooker and stir.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 3–4 hours or HIGH for 1½–2½ hours, until mushrooms are tender. They release liquid, so don't add more stock unless needed.\n4. If sauce is thin, stir in 1 tsp cornflour mixed with 1 tbsp cold water and cook on HIGH for 10 minutes. Turn off heat and stir in crème fraîche. Season and serve.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","3–4 hours on LOW","10 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker chickpea and spinach curry","2 x 400g tins chickpeas, drained; 1 onion (150g); 2 garlic cloves; 1 tbsp grated ginger; 3 tbsp curry paste; 400g chopped tomatoes; 400ml coconut milk; 150g baby spinach","1. Drain and rinse chickpeas. Chop onion and garlic; grate ginger.\n2. Add chickpeas, onion, garlic, ginger, curry paste, tomatoes and coconut milk to slow cooker. Stir well.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2–3 hours, until onion is soft and flavours meld.\n4. Stir in spinach for the final 10–20 minutes until wilted. Mash some chickpeas or cook uncovered on HIGH if sauce is thin. Season.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","4–5 hours on LOW","15 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker ratatouille","1 aubergine (300g); 2 courgettes (400g); 1 red pepper (150g); 1 onion (150g); 400g chopped tomatoes; 3 garlic cloves; 2 tsp dried oregano; 2 tbsp olive oil","1. Cut aubergine and courgettes into 2–3cm chunks; chop pepper and onion. Finely chop garlic.\n2. Toss vegetables with tomatoes, garlic, oregano and olive oil, then transfer to slow cooker. Season lightly.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2–3 hours, until vegetables are soft but still hold shape. Avoid stirring too often.\n4. Taste and adjust seasoning. If watery, cook uncovered on HIGH for 15–20 minutes. Serve with bread or rice.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","4–5 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker red cabbage and apple","1 red cabbage (about 800g); 2 apples (300g); 1 red onion (150g); 3 tbsp cider vinegar; 2 tbsp brown sugar; 1 tsp mixed spice; 100ml water","1. Remove tough outer leaves and core cabbage, then shred finely. Slice onion and apples.\n2. Mix vinegar, brown sugar, mixed spice and water in slow cooker. Add cabbage, apple and onion; toss thoroughly.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 5–6 hours or HIGH for 3–4 hours, stirring once or twice if practical, until tender.\n4. Balance with extra vinegar or sugar to taste. If excess liquid remains, cook uncovered on HIGH for 15–20 minutes.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/budget-slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW","15 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker chicken and leek pie filling","700g chicken thighs; 2 leeks (300g); 2 carrots (200g); 400ml chicken stock; 1 tsp dried thyme; 2 tbsp plain flour mixed with 3 tbsp cold water; 150g crème fraîche; 1 sheet ready-rolled puff pastry (about 320g)","1. Wash leeks carefully between layers and slice. Cut carrots into small chunks.\n2. Put chicken, leeks, carrots, stock and thyme in slow cooker. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C.\n3. Mix flour with cold water until smooth. Stir into hot liquid and cook on HIGH for 15–20 minutes until thickened. Stir in crème fraîche and season.\n4. Cool filling until no longer steaming. Spoon into pie dish, top with pastry and bake according to packet until pastry is golden and filling piping hot.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker pork and apple casserole","700g diced pork; 2 apples (300g); 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 300ml chicken stock; 1 tbsp wholegrain mustard; 1 tsp dried sage","1. Cut pork into 3cm chunks. Slice onion, cut carrots into chunks and core and chop apples.\n2. Brown pork in batches if possible and transfer to slow cooker.\n3. Add onion, carrots, apples, stock, mustard and sage. Stir well.\n4. Cover and cook on LOW for 7–8 hours or HIGH for 4–5 hours, until pork is tender and thoroughly cooked. Thicken sauce if needed; season and serve with mash.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","7–8 hours on LOW","20 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker honey roast ham","1–1.2kg gammon joint; 1 onion (150g); 250ml apple juice; 2 tbsp honey; 1 tbsp mustard; 1 tbsp brown sugar","1. Place sliced onion in slow cooker. Add gammon and apple juice; add a splash of water if needed so liquid reaches partway up the joint.\n2. Cover and cook on LOW for 6–8 hours, following pack and appliance guidance, until the centre reaches at least 70°C for 2 minutes or the pack's higher specified temperature.\n3. Lift out and rest for 10 minutes. Remove rind, leaving a thin layer of fat. Mix honey, mustard and brown sugar and brush over joint.\n4. Grill or roast at 200°C (180°C fan) for 10–15 minutes, watching closely, until sticky and golden. Rest before slicing.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","6–8 hours on LOW","10 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker chicken shawarma","800g chicken thighs; 1 onion (150g); 3 garlic cloves; 2 tsp ground cumin; 2 tsp paprika; 2 tsp ground coriander; 1 tsp ground turmeric; 100ml chicken stock; 2 tbsp lemon juice","1. Slice onion and finely chop garlic. Mix garlic, cumin, paprika, coriander, turmeric, lemon juice and stock.\n2. Put onion in slow cooker and arrange chicken thighs on top. Pour over spice mixture and turn chicken to coat.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C in the thickest part.\n4. Lift chicken out and slice or shred. For charred edges, spread on a tray and grill for 3–5 minutes, watching closely. Stir a little cooking juice through meat and serve in flatbreads.","https://www.bbc.com/food/collections/slow_cooker_recipes","5–6 hours on LOW","15 minutes"),
E("Slow cooker chicken and sweet potato stew","700g chicken thighs; 2 medium sweet potatoes (about 500g); 1 onion (150g); 2 carrots (200g); 400g chopped tomatoes; 300ml chicken stock; 1 tsp smoked paprika; 1 tsp dried thyme","1. Peel sweet potatoes and cut into 2cm cubes. Slice onion, cut carrots into chunks and cut chicken into large bite-sized pieces.\n2. Put sweet potato, onion, carrots, chicken, tomatoes, stock, paprika and thyme into slow cooker. Stir and season lightly.\n3. Cover and cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or HIGH for 2½–3 hours, until chicken reaches 75°C and sweet potato is tender. Avoid over-stirring.\n4. Taste and season. If stew is thin, mash a few sweet potato pieces into the liquid or cook uncovered on HIGH for 10–15 minutes.","https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/collection/slow-cooker-recipes","5–6 hours on LOW","15 minutes"),
 )
 fun all(): List<Recipe> = e.mapIndexed { i, r ->
  Recipe(id="slowcooker-curated-${i+1}",title=r.title,
   description="A complete slow-cooker recipe with measured ingredients and step-by-step instructions. Cooking times vary by appliance; check that meat is thoroughly cooked before serving.",
   ingredients=r.ingredients.replace("; ", "\n"),instructions=r.steps,sourceUrl=r.source,
   prepTime=r.prep,cookTime=r.cook,servings="4")
 }
}
